{
	"FileVersion": 3,
	"Version": 36,
	"VersionName": "1.20.0",
	"FriendlyName": "Create a Character System",
	"Description": "KH3-style compatible skeletons for FINAL FANTASY VII REBIRTH mods. A data object lists which skeletons play which skeletons' animations: Animations (KH3 mode), Mesh rebind, or Family (any number of skeletons share their animations both ways), with More Receiving Skeletons, Requires Paks, Adopt Paths and Carry Sockets; and, per character, which animations it plays: battle and field sets built from other characters' sets (with Auto Match of their attacks), moves and limit breaks (one animation or several played one after another), the ATB abilities and limit breaks of each animation pack the character switches to in battle (Create a Character System 3.3), socket stand-ins, kept proportions, field actions (written into the CharaSpec) and cutscenes. Build Moves makes a character's attacks from animations of the project (an imported or retargeted one per attack name, or a clip of one played faster or slower) with the gameplay notifies of the character's own animation of that name (damage, combo and cancel windows), lined up on the hit, plus a muzzle flash and gunshot for shots, and labels them for a chunk (46 by default). The Move Maker (Window > Rebirth Move Maker) makes one attack, ability or limit break at a time from any animation (another character's, the game's or an imported one, put on the character's skeleton keeping his build, keeping his own pose with the animation's motion added over an animation of his own such as his idle, or as that animation of his own leaning into the animation's root motion and moving as it does, for a monster on a person's walks and runs), with its hits set on the animation editor's playhead and each hit's own damage, effect and sound. Apply Socket Stand-ins puts the stand-ins on the project's meshes and Make Chain Assets makes AnimComposites of chained moves. Character Swaps put another character in some CharaSpec rows' place (Cloud in Sephiroth's): Apply To CharaSpec makes their packs spawn him with the voice you pick and their rows describe him (model, voice, effects, sounds, AI, his shared spec, the hand his weapon goes in), and Export Json makes the two skeletons a family (every character keeping its own height with Keep Proportions) and gives the rows the moveset you pick (the replaced character's or his own). Weapon Swaps put another weapon in a character's hands: Apply To CharaSpec makes the replaced weapons' CharaSpec rows describe the weapon their packs spawn (model, shared spec, effects and sounds), so cutscenes with them start, Export Json adds a weapon family so the new weapon plays the old one's cutscene animations, and socket stand-ins let the old weapon's moves hit with the new one. Forms (Create a Character System 3.6) give a character up to 13 forms it changes into in battle with a forms menu in the game's own menu art (hold Triangle, pick one, let go): each plays an animation pack with its own moves and abilities, and can show or hide parts of the model, wear another model with its AnimBlueprint and parts (Build Moves builds that form's moves on its skeleton, a model made facing another way or floating high turned and brought down with its Model Turn and Model Lift), hide the weapons, play effects and sounds as it switches, keep an aura and fly, and have super armor, a time limit shown on screen and a cooldown. Import Key Animations makes Anim Sequences on a skeleton from key animation files (.cacanim) the Create a Character System tools write for animations from other games. Flatten Root makes a skeleton whose export left a turn on its root bone (a Blender armature's rotation or another game's axes) rest its root flat like the game's own skeletons, keeping every pose, on its meshes and every animation, and can rename bones. Validate checks bones, curves, sockets, the game's bone-hierarchy test and the characters' CharaSpec rows, and shows how the game combines every compat file (Create a Character System 3.3 rules, with a preview of the auto matches); Export Json writes the Create a Character System UE4SS mod's JSON (Mesh rebind pairs can also go into the receiving skeleton's Asset User Data). Sound Banks (editor 1.14) make new sound banks for the game from WAV files (a character's own voice, new sound effects): Read Sound Bank WAVs fills a bank's lines from its WAV Folder (a folder per voice language for a voice bank), Build Sound Banks encodes them as the game's voice banks are (CRI HCA) into a SEAD sound bank and writes it as a ~mods container the game loads as it is, no cook needed. Skins (editor 1.15) are other models characters wear in game, each a folder of the game's own packages and a skin.json in place of a pak, any number installed at once: Build Skins cooks a skin's model (with its skeleton and physics asset) into the game's package format with the engine's IoStore, installs it into the game's Create a Character System folder and puts every installed skin into one ~mods container (CreateACharacterSkins_P); its skeleton joins the character's skeleton family, and a skin can bring its own voice and weapon (Create a Character System 3.10). The data object also has every newer game mod setting: a form's model put on the game's way (As Look), its own weapon, its set swaps, its voice, its cameras, its entrance and its shooter; a row's voice (Create a Character System 3.9: a character speaks with a bank of its own in some forms), Looks From (Toad turns the character into the slot owner's frog), AnimBlueprints From, cutscene weapon socket and shooter; socket stand-ins' own placement on their bones; pairs' proportion bones. The Remake Importer (editor 1.16) puts a FINAL FANTASY VII REMAKE model's sockets on its imported skeleton and mesh (RebirthRemakeImportLibrary.AddSockets): a weapon's Attach_Chara01, Body_Center01, muzzles; and writes animations as FBX files with a preview mesh of their skeleton (ExportAnimationsFbx, editor 1.16.2). The Skin Maker (editor 1.17: Window > Rebirth Skin Maker, or right-click a Skeletal Mesh > Create a Character Skin...) makes a skin from a model in a window of its own: its name, the characters that wear it (picked from the CharaSpec rows, every row of a character at once), its family, its voice and weapon (picked from the game's Customization catalog), model parts worn with it (a wing of its own), worn at once or a choice on the SKINS page; it keeps the skin in a data object (made the first time) and Build Skin builds that one skin into the game. The Parts Builder (Window > Rebirth Parts Builder, or right-click a Skeletal Mesh > Make a Customization Part...) makes a part of the Customization screen's PARTS page (another model on one of a character's bones, playing motions of its own: a wing, a tail, a halo) with a preview of it on a character playing its animations the way the game plays them (its own bone kept on the character's, its idle, KH3-style synced motions of the names of the character's, its motions for abilities, its sections and tint); Save Part puts it in the game's Customization catalog, Build Part also builds its model and animations of this project (with the game's compression) into the skins container. The AnimBlueprint Maker (editor 1.18: Window > Rebirth AnimBlueprint Maker, or right-click a Skeleton or Skeletal Mesh > Make a Rebirth AnimBlueprint...) makes a character's AnimBlueprint for the game from one of the game's own (Cloud's player AnimBlueprint by default; Sephiroth's, Vincent's, or the bosses' and summons' for a monster) for the character's skeleton: the template's field and battle locomotion, moves player, slots, facial, inertialization and expressions, its Control Rig off unless kept, written as a ~mods container (and installed), with the class path for a form's anim_class or a skin's anim_blueprint. Make Editable AnimBlueprint (editor 1.19) builds the template as an AnimBlueprint of this project for the skeleton instead, to edit like any AnimBlueprint: its AnimGraph with the game's End nodes (End's own AnimGraph nodes: behavior action, facial slot and lip sync, inertialization, movement and sword expressions, the locomotion sequence and blend space players), its locomotion state machine with every state, conduit and transition, the transitions' rules as nodes, its bindings and class defaults (without the Control Rig, which this editor cannot make); Cook For Game writes it as the ~mods container (and installs it). The Weapon Blueprint Maker (editor 1.20: Window > Rebirth Weapon Blueprint Maker, or right-click a Skeletal Mesh > Make a Rebirth Weapon Blueprint...) makes a weapon Blueprint for the game: a real Blueprint of this project made from one of the game's weapon blueprints (any of them: Cloud's Buster Sword, Sephiroth's cut-scale Masamune, Vincent's Quicksilver ...) with its native class as its parent (EndWeaponSkeletalMeshActor), its class defaults, its mesh component's settings and its own components (a gun's cartridges), holding your model; it keeps the game blueprint's name in a folder of its own, compiles and can be edited like any Blueprint (add effects, lights), and a skin whose Weapon names its class cooks it with its model, materials and textures.",
	"Category": "Editor",
